namespace GNM

/-- Positional tables of displacement permutations, in the convention of
`GN.finitePermutationValues`. For `4 ≤ k ≤ 21`, `0 ≤ j ≤ k` and `i < 3` the list
`permWitness k j i` has length `2 * k + 1`, and its entry at index `u + k`, for
`-k ≤ u ≤ k`, is `σ u + k + 1`, where `σ` is the `i`-th of three permutations of the
interval `[-k, k]` with `j` removed whose displacements `σ u - u` take every nonzero
value of `[-k, k]` exactly once; the entry at the hole index `u = j` carries `j + k + 1`.
Outside that range the list is empty. The three permutations listed at each `(k, j)` are
distinct, and every property claimed of these tables is established by kernel-checked
computations in the modules that use them. -/
